> Viruses are "restricted" in their host range because hosts have enzymes
> that cut DNA at specific sequences that may or not appear in the virus
> genome, but which appear nowhere in the host genome.  When the
enzymes are
> harvested and applied to experimental sample DNA, the cut pieces are
called
> "restriction fragments", and variations (polymorphism) in cut
points, and
> thus the fragment lengths, are a sign that different kinds of DNA are in
> the sample.
